  "heading": "H ::= (X', *', e') \\:subgroup:/ G ::= (X, *, e)",
  "heading_latex": "H\\textrm{ is a subgroup of }G\\quad\\htmlClass{mlg-title-written}{H \\leq G}",
  "parameter_destructurings": [
    "H ::= \\left(X', *', e'\\right)",
    "G ::= \\left(X, \\ast, e\\right)"
  ],
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[H ::= (X', *', e') \\:subgroup:/ G ::= (X, *, e)]\nDefines: H ::= (X', *', e')\nwhen: G is \\group\nextends: H is \\set via X'\nmeans:\n. X' \\:(nonempty)::set.theoretic.subset:/ X\n. *' is \\binary.operation:on{X'}\n. e' \"in\" X'\nsatisfies:\n. (.*' := \\restriction:of{`*`}:on{X' \\.set.cross./ X'}.)[:1:]\n. have:\n  . forAll: x, y \"in\" H\n    then:\n    . x *' y \"in\" H\n    . x *' y = x * y\n  . forAll: x \"in\" H\n    then: x.inv \"in\" H\n  asserting: H is \\group\nDocumented:\n. called: \"$H?$ is a subgroup of $G?$\"\n. written: \"H? \\leq G?\"\n. description: \"A subgroup $H \\leq G$ is a nonempty subset of $G$ that is closed\n                under the group operation and under taking inverses, and whose\n                operation is the restriction of that of $G$. Under these\n                conditions $H$ is again a group in its own right.\"\nJustification:\n. [1]\n  have: *' := \\restriction:of{`*`}:on{X' \\.set.cross./ X'}\n  asserting: (.X' \\.set.cross./ X'.) \\:set.theoretic.subset?:/ (.G \\.set.cross./ G.)\n  because: X' \\:set.theoretic.subset?:/ X\n  by: \\cross.of.subset.is.subset.of.cross#given{X := X; Y := X'}\nId: \"d8fe82d3-6f50-4711-ad64-76d4eb0615ff\"",
